{"id":"nchi-7bb337","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-09d441b0-5199-4803-a9b2-53a588cde7c5","text":"Implemented per spec with the user's rule (any agent that needs you wins over the new one). Not committed yet; the branch build is running for the user to try.\n\n- `AgentAdapter.perform` and `AgentStore.perform` return `AgentRef?` (`@discardableResult`):\n  - Herdr: the pane from `layout.apply`\n  - Mock: the agent it adds\n  - Claude Code: nil\n- `AgentStore.select(_:yieldsToAnyUrgent:)` adds `selectionYields`. `AgentsState.primary`/`others` take `yields:`: a yielding selection gives way to *any* other agent that needs attention, and comes back once none does. Chip clicks are unchanged.\n- The new chat (`NotchModel.sendPrompt`) and the folder drop (`NotchController.startAgent`) select the started agent with `yieldsToAnyUrgent: true`.\n- Tests:\n  - reducer: `aStartedAgentGivesWayToAnyAgentThatNeedsYou`, covering selection before the agent appears, an already-waiting agent winning, the agent coming back, and the new agent asking itself\n  - store: `startReportsTheNewAgentAndSelectingItMakesItPrimary`\n  - Herdr integration: each start returns a distinct pane that exists\n- 140 tests pass."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T08:10:40.053441Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
